 "BINDING": {
  "BOARD_SCHEMA_FINDING": {
   "disposition": "the derivation is disclosed per board via TEAMS_DERIVED_FROM_GAME_KEY rather than performed silently. Carrying away/home as fields on the MLB board is the real fix and is NOT applied here \u2014 the 8/28 board is frozen under R3.",
   "how_it_surfaced": "the first pass through the gate refused all 15 MLB rows with MISSING_IDENTITY_FIELD twice per row, while all 4 WNBA rows bound cleanly. The asymmetry is the board schema, not the relay.",
   "severity": "BOUNDED. It does NOT make binding circular against an archive row, which carries its own away/home \u2014 TEAMS_REVERSED can still fire there. The narrow exposure is that if a game key were ever BUILT backwards at freeze time, nothing on the board could contradict it, because the board holds no second copy to disagree with. That is the same shape as the LAD@DET starter reversal: one source, nothing to disagree with it.",
   "teams_derived_from_game_key": {
    "mlb": 15,
    "wnba": 0
   },
   "what": "the MLB board stores away and home ONLY inside the composite game key (\"mlb:CIN@CHC\"). The WNBA board stores them as explicit fields. Two of the six fields in the binding contract are therefore not independently held on an MLB board and must be parsed back out of the identifier."
  },
